it was shortly after delivering a eulogy  at the memorial service for former  president f w de clarke when south  african president sular maposa fell ill  he is one of more than 18 thousand  people in the country who have  contracted covert 19 in the past 24  hours  the government says the president is  suffering mild symptoms and is being  monitored  those who've had close contact with  ramaphosa have been told to isolate in a  tweet issued by the president while  thanking people for their support he  urged all south africans to get  vaccinated  so far 43 percent of eligible south  africans have received at least one jab  while there is enough stock available  including booster shots many people are  still reluctant to get a jab the  government says it's trying to dispel  misinformation and create greater  awareness about the importance of being  vaccinated  but many other countries in africa have  not had the same access to vaccines  just seven percent of africa's more than  one billion population has been  inoculated against  have coronavirus really been  disappointed  in the approach that the rich countries  have taken on the issue of vaccines  firstly they hoarded our seeds  they ordered more vaccines than their  populations required  and when we wanted vaccines  they just kept you know giving us the  crumbs from their table  in the last week an average of 19 000  south africans have been infected every  day  health experts say the surge could be  driven by the new omicron variant but  although they say it's highly contagious  preliminary data indicates it may not  cause severe illness  and while the government may be directed  by science a fully vaccinated but ill  president may do little to reassure  those already skeptical of being jabbed  family al jazeera johannesburg
 

